      "text": "Concentration of Submodular Functions and Read-k Families Under Negative Dependence — We study the question of whether submodular functions of random variables satisfying various notions of negative\n\n**Concentration of Submodular Functions and Read-k Families Under Negative Dependence**\n\n19 pp, 13 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** We study the question of whether submodular functions of random variables satisfying various notions of negative dependence satisfy Chernoff-like concentration inequal- ities. We prove such a concentration inequality for the lower tail when the random variables satisfy negative association or negative regression, partially resolving an open problem raised in ([1]). Previous work showed such concentration results for random variables that come from speciﬁc dependent-rounding algorithms ([2, 3]). We discuss some applications of our results to combinatorial optimization and beyond. We also show applications to the concentration of read-k families [4] under certain forms of negative dependence; we further show a simpliﬁed proof of the entropy-method approach of [4].\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; Concentration of Submodular Functions and Read; Abstract; 1 Introduction; 2 Preliminaries; 2.1 Notions of Negative Dependence; 2.2 Submodular Functions; 3 Submodular Chernoff Bounds; 3.1 1-Negative Association and Weak Negative R; 3.2 Proof of Submodular Concentration; 3.3 Concentration of read-k families; Acknowledgements; References",
